@startuml usecase
left to right direction
title Figure 6  Use Case Diagram — Actors and the Nine Use Cases\n(the phase P0–P4 in which each use case runs is shown in the ellipse; agents are not modelled here)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 20
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 30
skinparam ranksep 90
skinparam usecase {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #333333
}
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #333333
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
}

' ================= Actor: the human user, on the left =================
actor "RCA\n(Registered\nCompany Auditor)" as RCA

' ================= Actors: external parties, on the right =================
actor "Client\n(audited entity: management\nand those charged\nwith governance)" as CL
actor "External Data Source\n(ASIC Connect / ABN Lookup,\naccounting systems,\nconfirmation platform)" as EXT
actor "EQR Reviewer" as EQR

' ================= System boundary =================
rectangle "Audit Support System" as SYS {
  usecase "UC-01\nEngagement acceptance\n(P0)" as UC01
  usecase "UC-02\nPlanning and risk assessment\n(P1)" as UC02
  usecase "UC-03\nProcedure execution and\nfull-population JE testing\n(P2)" as UC03
  usecase "UC-04\nException review and\njudgment confirmation\n(P2)" as UC04
  usecase "UC-05\nRisk re-assessment\n(P2 -> P1)" as UC05
  usecase "UC-06\nCompletion evaluation and\nreport generation\n(P3 -> P4)" as UC06
  usecase "UC-07\nArchiving and\nengagement switch\n(P4 -> Archived)" as UC07
  usecase "UC-08\nProgress and\nprovenance enquiry\n(any phase)" as UC08
  usecase "UC-09\nStatutory notification\nand withdrawal\n(any phase)" as UC09
}

' ================= Associations: left actors =================
RCA -- UC01
RCA -- UC02
RCA -- UC03 : manual-engine\nprocedures
RCA -- UC04
RCA -- UC05
RCA -- UC06
RCA -- UC07
RCA -- UC08
RCA -- UC09

UC01 -- CL : engagement letter,\nmanagement undertakings
UC02 -- CL : draft statements,\ndocuments, further data
UC06 -- CL : response on misstatements,\nadjusting entries,\nrepresentation letter
UC05 -- CL : governance discussion\nafter a fraud trigger (GEN-16)
UC09 -- CL : NOCLAR discussion,\ngovernance response\n(GEN-13, EthicsBreach)

UC01 -- EXT : ASIC registration,\nABN validity,\ncourt records
UC02 -- EXT : accounting\nsystem feed
UC03 -- EXT : confirmations (A5),\naccounting data
UC04 -- EXT : evidence for\nadditional procedures (A5)
UC06 -- EXT : adjusting entries\nvia API
UC09 -- EXT : lodgement in the\nprescribed form

UC06 -- EQR : pre-signature review\n[eqr_required]
UC07 -- EQR : read-only access\nto the archive

' ================= Explicit use case relations =================
UC05 .[norank].> UC04 : <<extend>> (a)
UC09 .[norank].> UC05 : <<extend>> (b)
UC09 .[norank].> UC02 : <<extend>> (c)
UC09 .[norank].> UC04 : <<extend>> (d)
UC09 .[norank].> UC06 : <<extend>> (e)

' ================= Notes =================

' ================= Legend =================
legend right
  |= Notation |= Meaning |
  | actor to use case | association; the label states what the actor supplies or receives |
  | <<extend>> | conditional insertion; the arrow points from the extending use case to the base, guard letter on the arrow |
  | (a) | uncorrected misstatements exceed 70% of overall materiality |
  | (b) | GATE-R decision = withdraw |
  | (c) | AwaitingData retries exhausted -> ACC-10 |
  | (d) | NOCLAR found, or management refuses to remove a scope limitation |
  | (e) | FIN-18 representations unreliable, or FIN-10 independence breach |
  | (P0 … P4) | phase of the main state machine (12.3) in which the use case runs |
  |= Rule |= |
  | Single entry | every human interaction passes through A10; agents are not shown inside the boundary |
  | Actor scope | Client supplies data, documents and letters and answers enquiries and communications as management or governance; External Data Source covers registry, accounting and confirmation interfaces and statutory lodgement |
  | Guard, not a relation | an undecided statutory notification in UC-09 blocks RPT-01 in UC-06 (M-12) |
  | Trigger, not a relation | UC-02 to UC-03, UC-06 to UC-07, and queue-driven entry into UC-04 are state transitions |
  | UC-03 | started automatically by the P1 -> P2 transition; RCA performs the manual-engine procedures inside it, A5 reaches the confirmation platform |
  | UC-07 extension points | workpaper added after archiving -> Amended; facts known after the report date -> RPT-11 PostReportFacts re-opens P3 ReExecuting, then P4 |
endlegend

' ================= Layout =================
CL -[hidden]right- EXT
EXT -[hidden]right- EQR
UC01 -[hidden]left- UC02
UC02 -[hidden]left- UC03
UC03 -[hidden]left- UC04
UC04 -[hidden]left- UC06
UC06 -[hidden]left- UC07
UC07 -[hidden]left- UC08
UC05 -[hidden]left- UC09
UC04 -[hidden]down-> UC05
UC06 -[hidden]down-> UC09
@enduml
